  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given an integer NNN, output the NthN^{th}Nth term in the Fibonacci Series.\n\nThe Fibonacci Series is: `0 1 1 2 3 5 8...`\n\nComplete the function `fib()` function to solve this problem using **recursion**.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe input contains a single integer NNN.\n\n\nOutput Format\nOutput the NthN^{th}Nth term in the Fibonacci Series.",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= T <= 10",
      "1 <= N <= 30",
      "All values are integers"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "First line contains T, the number of test cases. Each test case contains a single integer N.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print the Nth term of the Fibonacci series on a new line.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\n1",
        "output": "0",
        "explanation": "There is one test case. N=1 corresponds to the first element of the series, which is 0."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\n2",
        "output": "1",
        "explanation": "One test case with N=2. The second element of the Fibonacci series is 1."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\n7",
        "output": "8",
        "explanation": "One test case with N=7. The series up to the 7th term is 0,1,1,2,3,5,8; thus the 7th term is 8."
      }
